Tolerate SPI reply misses in bursts instead of aborting the controller manager.

Upstream candle throws "Fatal communication error!" from its own update
thread after 5 consecutive missed replies from the CANdle HAT; nothing can
catch it, so ros2_control_node aborts and the robot is down for the ~30 s the
watchdog needs to restart the stack.  On Wojtek the SPI link to the HAT drops
replies in bursts of up to ~20 per second (supply dips), and the MD80 driver
already declares "Drive link lost" itself after link_stall_cycles (1 s at
200 Hz) of no fresh data, which is the recovery path that should decide.
deploy.sh applies this on top of the pinned CANDLE_COMMIT.

diff --git a/include/bus.hpp b/include/bus.hpp
index 05246dd..b4fcbde 100644
--- a/include/bus.hpp
+++ b/include/bus.hpp
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ class Bus
 	bool manageMsgErrors(bool ret);
 
    private:
-	static const uint32_t errorThreshold = 5;
+	static const uint32_t errorThreshold = 100;
 	static const uint32_t msgCntThreshold = 1000;
 	uint32_t msgCnt = 0;
 	uint32_t errorCnt = 0;
